                {
                  "key": "q",
                  "value": "",
                  "disabled": true,
                  "description": "Free text matched case-insensitively anywhere in the session's name. LIKE wildcards in the term are escaped, so `50%` searches for those characters rather than matching everything."
                },
                {
                  "key": "limit",
                  "value": "20",
                  "disabled": false,
                  "description": ""
                },
                {
                  "key": "offset",
                  "value": "0",
                  "disabled": false,
                  "description": "Rows to skip. Ordering is a total order (`started_at DESC, id`), so paging is deterministic against an unchanging set. It is not stable across writes: a session added while you page shifts every later row down one, so a row can repeat. Use the date filters to pin a range if that matters."
